      "raw": "<p>No.&nbsp; You only ditch your cards in play (and hand and trash and deck) when you&#39;re actually incapacitated.&nbsp; The Aegis replaces the instance of lethal damage entirely with &quot;set your current HP to 10, then destroy the Aegis&quot;.&nbsp; (Note that this happens even if a Fixed Point is in play, which would prevent you from actually being incapacitated at 0 HP...conveniently, it also prevents you from destroying the Aegis, so you just get to go up to 10 HP with no downside, even though losing your last HP wouldn&#39;t actually kill you that round.)</p>",
